  "name": "Electron gun",
  "description": "An electron gun: the hot cathode (left) gives at most 0.1 per unit length of its face (its temperature limits it: a stronger field pulls no more), the anode's slit lets a thin beam through, and the small collector on the right should catch it. But the beam's electrons repel one another: it spreads and misses. Place two plates beside the beam to focus it, so that at least 0.08 reaches the collector (averaged over $t = 20$ to $40$). A plate at a lower potential than the beam's surroundings pushes the electrons back toward the axis; too low, and it throws them back.",
